{"kind":"report","text":"CHECKER VERDICT (as report; the guarded review is blocked because every artifact for this head carries the 7-character commit 385ff5c - see assert 6e38d078; republish with 385ff5ce374b691d00099be2a829cf04d2f1d636 and re-request) for the signed GitHub release distribution at exact commit 385ff5ce374b691d00099be2a829cf04d2f1d636: CHANGES REQUESTED. VERIFIED: clean worktree go vet OK, go test 14 ok, go test -race 14 ok, scripts/demo.sh exit 0, sh -n clean, markdown links clean; stamp_test and buildinfo tests cover the validated semver stamp; scripts/release.sh executed locally with v0.0.0-check into a temp dir produced the four darwin/linux arm64/amd64 archives with CGO_ENABLED=0 (pure-Go ncruces sqlite, so cross-compilation is sound), checksums.txt verified with shasum -a 256 -c, the darwin/arm64 archive extracted and its tailapp ran. Workflow audit: trigger is push of tags v* only (no pull_request, no branch push), so PR and branch traffic cannot publish; the semver gate re-derives the tag with git describe --exact-match and validates a strict semver regex identical to release.sh and build.sh; permissions are the minimum for the job (contents:write for gh release create, id-token:write for keyless Cosign OIDC, attestations:write); ordering is verify source -\u003e build archives -\u003e cosign sign-blob checksums (bundle + sig) -\u003e attest-build-provenance on the archives -\u003e gh release create, so nothing is published before it is signed and attested; docs verify-blob identity regexp is anchored to this workflow path at refs/tags/v* with the GitHub OIDC issuer, and gh attestation verify is given as the independent path; gh release create refuses an existing release; no long-lived secret. REQUIRED: R1 archive contents - each tar contains only the tailapp binary; the project is Apache-2.0 with a NOTICE file, and Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires NOTICE to accompany redistributions, so include LICENSE and NOTICE (and ideally a short README pointing at docs/reference/releases.md) in every archive and say so in releases.md. R2 tag gating - any commit a pusher tags is released, including an unreviewed branch commit; add a step after checkout that requires the tagged commit to be reachable from main (git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD origin/main, fetch-depth 0 is already set) and state in releases.md that releases are cut only from merged main. ADVISORIES: A1 actions are tag-pinned (checkout@v7, setup-go@v7, cosign-installer@v3, attest-build-provenance@v2); pin to commit SHAs for supply-chain integrity, matching the earlier advisory on ci.yml. A2 the archives are not reproducible despite the deterministic header comment: tar embeds mtimes and gzip a timestamp; use tar --mtime with a fixed epoch (or the tag commit time) and gzip -n, or drop the word deterministic. A3 the checksum manifest is signed but the archive names inside it are not tied to the tag beyond the version string; fine, but the provenance attestation already covers that - mention it. A4 consider a dry-run job on pull requests that runs release.sh without signing or publishing so packaging breaks are caught before a tag. PROVENANCE NOTE for the operator: this feature was builder self-filed (promise 0fbb751c) with no operator direction on record; nothing here changes runtime behavior, but the operator should sanction or decline the release process itself."}